    "body": "- [x] I have read the [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) file.\r\n- [x] I have read the [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) file.\r\n\r\nUsually, iPhones have `dng` and `heic` filetypes for images. This PR adds icon support for those as well.\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2024-07-07T11:06:35Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nI am afraid both 'heic' and 'dng' extensions don't really fit the [criteria for making them built-in](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/45b3540003566e8f19c4cc4b1c9d0b8605a2697c/doc/mini-icons.txt#L297-L298). In particular, they don't really seem to be popular (at least, this is the first time *I* am hearing about them) and they seem mostly tied to language/software (this is not present in criteria for extensions, but it is for \"file\" and \"directory\"; I'll fix that).\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
            "created_at": "2024-07-07T11:06:35Z",
